Subject: [PATCH] cca2-ett resolution edit LE-gate23: correct argument order in
 three docstrings (G23-02)

Codex finding G23-02: three documentation references gave argument lists
that disagree with the declarations. Docstrings and module docs only.

- Reduction.lean, dAbs_eq: `dAbs q E hE b n s` -> `dAbs E hE q b n s`
  (the section variables E hE precede q b n; as in the statement).
- Handler.lean, module Main definitions: `dHandler E hE q b` ->
  `dHandler q E hE b` (q is the file-level variable; as at every use).
- CPAHandler.lean, module Main definitions: `bHandler q hq b` ->
  `bHandler q` (q is its only parameter; as at every use).

Sweep of the other EncryptThenTag doc comments for dAbs, dHandler,
bHandler and bAbs: one more of the same kind, fixed:
- CPAReduction.lean, comp_bAbs: `bAbs ((o, L), j)` -> `bAbs q n ((o, L), j)`
  (as in the bAbs and bAbs_eq docstrings and the statement).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PqpVTiuDcjSqhyfbqnsVxA
